# This project pins next@12 while @next/third-parties@14 declares a peer
# dependency on next 13/14, so strict peer resolution (npm 7+) fails with
# ERESOLVE. Vercel's builder happened to install anyway, which meant
# `npm ci` / `npm install` failed locally and in CI while production builds
# succeeded — the exact divergence that lets a broken tree reach production.
# Make the lenient resolution explicit so every environment installs the same
# way.
legacy-peer-deps=true
